RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.entrypoints, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
Initialized the measurement profile and time-allocation plan after reading the immutable evaluator, task parquet metadata, living table notes, and feature history.
ABANDONED direct full residual-token ablation after training-only forward folds underperformed the simpler pooled ridge; optional LoRA rerun was stopped before producing new artifacts.
Implemented five temporally censored BiomedBERT fields, separate 2020/2021 corpus banks, two-layer four-head contrastive set pooling, masked-field reconstruction, graph-linked positives, chronological rank-8 LoRA checkpoints, same-phase/year hard negatives, 32-trial semantic and exact-link retrieval, gated evidence fusion, BCE plus same-timestamp pairwise ranking, modality dropout, and separate validation/test model chains.
Added all-table structured residuals, within-seed normalization, historical empirical-Bayes priors, nonlinear age/design basis terms, multi-prefix evidence summaries, an OOF-selected strongly regularized ridge head, and a training-only 20% frozen-field probe blend.
Measured full bank throughput at 1,151-1,417 chunks/second; full initial bank construction completed in 37 minutes. Stage A reached 0.70390 pooled training OOF AUC; Stage B reached 0.67419 and was rejected by a -0.02971 delta versus 0.00736 paired uncertainty.
The immutable evaluator directory was read but not modified; the system-provided registered evaluation remains kapso_evaluation/kapso_eval.py.
Recovered difficulties: DuckDB rejected aliases `year`, `value`, and `key` as reserved words; aliases were renamed. The prediction checker ignored a positional path and initially searched kapso_output; setting KAPSO_RUN_DATA_DIR fixed the invocation. Pairwise sparse augmentation raised `TypeError: sparse array length is ambiguous`; using matrix.shape[0] fixed it before the feature was ultimately rejected.
Registered full evaluation archived run_0008: average_precision=0.7664996260, accuracy=0.6322916667, f1=0.7367636092, roc_auc=0.6939943441.
Post-evaluation resolution diagnostic on campaign-best run_0002: 100-draw bootstrap SE=0.015897; six non-duplicate materially different candidates had mean rank correlation=0.8433 and scores 0.67908-0.70667, all within two SE. Validation volume/rate were 960/0.5844 versus 2019 train 1093/0.6029 and test volume 825.
Recovered diagnostic difficulty: an initial validation slice join lost task row order and produced impossible near-0.48 slice AUCs; carrying an explicit row_index through DuckDB and sorting before attaching predictions restored correct 0.66-0.74 major-slice AUCs.
RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas
Won the atomic replay lock, copied and hash-verified the orphan champion, restored its 217 structured plus 96 retrieval plus 48/32 PCA implementation, and archived its maintained five-window replay as run_0009 with mean ROC-AUC 0.7060061454.
Exported canonical purged 2016-2019 fold identities and generated row-validated OOF predictions for the locked orphan LightGBM/ridge family, depth-4 ontology CatBoost family, and three-seed epoch-2 dual-view BiomedBERT/317-tree sidecar family.
Implemented nested equal-rank, simplex, and nonnegative L2-logistic combiners, paired-year uncertainty, sponsor-blocked bootstrap, and low-site/sparse-history gates without using official 2020 labels.
Selected the simplex rank ensemble with weights 0.3/0.1/0.6 after a +0.013448 mean OOF gain, 4/4 positive years, paired SE 0.002309, 2019 gain +0.010659, low-site gain +0.018906, and sparse-history gain +0.018067.
Preserved separate official Model-A validation and Model-B test family vectors, stored fingerprinted prediction banks for every maintained evaluation origin, and validated full shapes, order, finiteness, and bounds.
External models: NeuML/pubmedbert-base-embeddings and the archived BiomedBERT encoder were reused only on sanitized trial text. No external row-level clinical-trial data was added.
Evaluation suite changes: none by this implementation; the pre-existing maintainer-owned multi-window evaluator was read and executed without modification.
Recovered difficulty: the first replay checksum file embedded its temporary staging path, so verification failed after atomic rename; regenerating SHA256SUMS with relative names fixed the artifact.
Recovered difficulty: historical validation rows contain the same cohort as official training-year folds in a different positional order; direct equality failed at 2016, and explicit nct_id mapping restored exact labels and all per-year AUCs.
Recovered difficulty: the run_0004 archived modeling module predates rejected_widening_columns, raising AttributeError; using the v3 matrix and directly excluding relative and prototype columns reproduced the specified 322-column CatBoost configuration.
Recovered difficulty: the first detached LM OOF job exited before producing output, and a foreground diagnostic exposed model-loading progress bars; restarting with transformer progress disabled and incremental per-seed caches completed all missing folds.
Measured cache assumption discrepancy: a reproduced 2018 seed-17 LM fold had correlation 0.977612 with the cached vector but a different hash and maximum absolute difference 0.169922, consistent with nondeterministic GPU training; row IDs, labels, cutoff, configuration, and length matched, so the original valid cached prediction remained selected.
